# Auto-generated session reports, written by ~/.claude/hooks/session-report.sh.
# Ignored rather than tracked, and the distinction is not "planning files are
# noise" — `.planning/.continue-here.md` and `.planning/HANDOFF.json` ARE tracked,
# because they are hand-curated state that nothing else records.
#
# A session report is DERIVED: "9 commits from last 24h" is recomputable from
# `git log` and disagrees with it the moment anything moves. Versioning a
# derived snapshot beside the source it was derived from creates two answers to
# one question, and the stale one looks authoritative.
#
# Both conventions exist across ~/projetos (3 repos ignore, ~9 track), so this
# is a choice for this repo, not a house rule — reverting is deleting these lines.
.planning/reports/

# SwarmVault scaffolding. `swarmvault` (a global knowledge-vault CLI) drops a
# generic config, a schema template and five empty directories into whatever
# directory it is pointed at — it did so here on 2026-09-02, and the config is
# byte-identical to the one in ~/projetos. Nothing in this blog reads any of
# it. Ignored rather than deleted: the files belong to that tool, not to this
# repo, and removing another tool's state is its owner's call.
swarmvault.config.json
swarmvault.schema.md
/raw/
/wiki/
/state/
/agent/
/inbox/
